1
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:03,629
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,926
[grinding]

3
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:44,563
Truly, Luomen,
you are impressive. Oh.

4
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:47,733
You make the art of medicine
look so effortless.

5
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,152
That's only because I have

6
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,820
such a competent assistant,
Guen.

7
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:53,447
Do you mean it?

8
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,365
-Maybe I help.
-[kitten meows]

9
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:57,367
But you deserve all the credit.

10
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:59,244
I do miss the girl
and her friend,

11
00:01:59,328 --> 00:02:00,912
but they finished their tenures.

12
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:02,247
-[door opens]
-Hmm?

13
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:04,624
Excuse me.

14
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:06,543
This is for Master Guen.

15
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:09,838
Oh? What could it be?

16
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:12,799
Hmm?

17
00:02:14,009 --> 00:02:14,885
Hmm.

18
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,347
[Maomao sighs]

19
00:02:20,057 --> 00:02:22,225
I knew it was
only a matter of time.

20
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:23,810
Master Jinshi always manages

21
00:02:23,894 --> 00:02:26,646
to find some new
bothersome issue to bring up.

22
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:29,191
And it's not like
I can turn down his request.

23
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:30,817
[sighs]

24
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:37,616
I'll have to come up
with some way to convince Grams.

25
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:45,707
-[Kyou-u chuckles]
-Huh?

26
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:48,085
-Mugwort? Yum!
-[Zulin humming]

27
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:49,961
Dumplings? Yum!

28
00:02:50,045 --> 00:02:51,463
-Put 'em together...
-[gasps]

29
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,423
-...that's yum in my tum.
-[MAOMAO] Hold it right there!

30
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:54,508
-Ah!
-[Zulin gasps]

31
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:55,926
[KYOU-U] Hey,
what are you doing?

32
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:57,052
-[MAOMAO] Hmm.
-[Kyou-u gasps]

33
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:00,305
If you didn't
nearly kill yourself,

34
00:03:00,389 --> 00:03:02,599
I'd be impressed you
miraculously found wolfsbane

35
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:04,226
-in these parts.
-What?

36
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:06,019
It looks
just like mugwort, though.

37
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,437
But it's not.

38
00:03:07,938 --> 00:03:09,773
A snack made of these
will be your last.

39
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:13,068
But my dumplings!
What about them?

40
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:15,237
-All dreams die.
-[groans]

41
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:18,240
Hang on.
You found some yesterday.

42
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:20,242
How about sharing
some of your mugwort with us?

43
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:23,036
-Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.
-I need it for moxibustion.

44
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,246
Stingy.

45
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,331
[both groan]

46
00:03:26,415 --> 00:03:28,208
[KYOU-U]
You're the meanest ever!

47
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:29,793
I saved your lives.

48
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:32,754
How many times have I said
not to wander off by yourselves?

49
00:03:33,797 --> 00:03:35,006
We weren't alone.

50
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:36,633
Sazen was with us.

51
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:37,634
Huh?

52
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:40,011
[SAZEN] Don't leave me behind!

53
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:42,889
I'm not as young
as I used to be.

54
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,642
[MAOMAO] Well, this brat's
never gonna learn,

55
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:48,228
which means I'll have to
teach the chaperone instead.

56
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,690
You all wait right here.

57
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:52,774
[Sazen panting]

58
00:03:54,276 --> 00:03:55,777
[ALL] Huh?

59
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:57,863
[MAOMAO] Look.

60
00:03:58,488 --> 00:03:59,739
You see a difference?

61
00:03:59,823 --> 00:04:01,992
[ALL] Hmm.

62
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:05,245
I suppose.
One's mugwort, one's wolfsbane.

63
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:06,496
[MAOMAO] Huh?

64
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:09,916
I was going to swap them later,
but he ran off with the basket.

65
00:04:09,999 --> 00:04:11,710
I shouldn't even give you these.

66
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,670
But here you go.

67
00:04:13,754 --> 00:04:15,881
-[both gasp]
-You saved our dumplings!

68
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:17,799
-[both chuckling excitedly]
-[KYOU-U] Let's go!

69
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,095
[SAZEN] I brought this
back for you.

70
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,264
Found some wolfsbane root.

71
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:26,725
I pulled it up
because it's dangerous,

72
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:29,853
but recalled it can be used
in medicine if allowed to dry.

73
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,146
Right? Here.

74
00:04:31,855 --> 00:04:33,774
Shouldn't waste aconiti tuber.

75
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,359
[MAOMAO] Is this
some kind of prank?

76
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:37,777
How does he know the name

77
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:39,946
for the medicinal form
of wolfsbane root?

78
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:42,032
My guess?

79
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,742
Someone probably brought it
down the mountain

80
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,203
because the flower was pretty,
and didn't realize how deadly--

81
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,121
[exclaims]

82
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,873
♪

83
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,503
What's this one?

84
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:56,421
Uh, medlar leaf.

85
00:04:56,505 --> 00:04:58,048
Its effects?

86
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:00,759
It can stop coughing fits
and diarrhea.

87
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:01,927
At least, I think.

88
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,178
[MAOMAO] And this?

89
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:05,472
[SAZEN] Goldthread.
Good for the stomach.

90
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,933
And mental stability, I believe.

91
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,017
[MAOMAO] And over here.

92
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,477
[SAZEN] Plantain, of course.

93
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:13,355
My turn now. What is this about?

94
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:14,773
We're not done yet.

95
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:16,316
Huh?

96
00:05:18,068 --> 00:05:19,903
[MAOMAO] Out of all the plants
I showed you,

97
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,822
you were familiar
with about half.

98
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:24,407
Are you finally
going to explain?

99
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:25,450
In time.

100
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:26,618
You were taught to read?

101
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,411
Huh? Yeah.

102
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:30,247
By the old man
at the stronghold.

103
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,665
Is that all?

104
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,708
Or did he teach you
about herbs too?

105
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:34,751
He did.

106
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:36,753
How perfect.

107
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:38,630
I didn't see this coming.

108
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:41,341
It'll be a rush job,
but it just might work.

109
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:42,801
-Here.
-Huh?

110
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:43,760
Memorize this book.

111
00:05:44,636 --> 00:05:45,804
From now on,

112
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,264
you're gonna work with me
during the day.

113
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:49,224
Huh? I already have a job!

114
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:52,269
I'll explain the situation
to Grams and Ukyou myself.

115
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,980
And anyway, when it comes to
being a manservant,

116
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,439
you're not the best out there.

117
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:57,649
[gasps]

118
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:59,359
Well, I try, but...

119
00:05:59,985 --> 00:06:03,363
Maybe you're better suited
to being an apothecary.

120
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:06,658
Thanks to my connection
with Master Jinshi,

121
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,660
I'll be away
from this place often.

122
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:11,580
But if Sazen can take on my role
while I'm gone...

123
00:06:13,582 --> 00:06:15,458
[SAZEN] I started off
as a simple farmer.

124
00:06:16,293 --> 00:06:17,877
The only reason
I went to the stronghold

125
00:06:17,961 --> 00:06:19,337
was because I was broke.

126
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,258
[sighs]

127
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:28,096
Uh? Ah!

128
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,764
All I meant by that was

129
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:32,309
I was simply following
the old man's instructions.

130
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:33,852
-Why's that matter?
-Huh?

131
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:36,021
There are people
who make a decent living

132
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:38,607
casting strange curses
on patients with colds.

133
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,526
You, on the other hand,
can create a cure for a fever.

134
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:44,237
If I had to, sure.

135
00:06:44,321 --> 00:06:45,739
But what about
the seriously ill?

136
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,115
Be honest.

137
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:49,242
If it's beyond your skills,
just tell them so.

138
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:50,327
Huh?

139
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:53,079
Whether or not
they take medicine,

140
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,539
some people will die.

141
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,999
Pass them off to someone else.

142
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:58,627
Better than pretending
you have a cure.

143
00:06:58,710 --> 00:06:59,669
You'd be surprised

144
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,297
how many doctors are worse
at making medicine than you.

145
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,299
Like a certain quack.

146
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:06,384
So it's settled then.

147
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,055
[Sazen gasps]

148
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,598
I'll go talk to Grams.

149
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:13,475
Read these while I'm gone.

150
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:17,062
Don't you think this is all
moving a little fast?

151
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:19,648
We have to move fast,
or we'll run out of time.

152
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:24,653
As I expected,

153
00:07:25,236 --> 00:07:27,489
Sazen turned out
to be a quick study.

154
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:30,116
He was able to learn
simple recipes quickly.

155
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,284
Best of all,

156
00:07:31,368 --> 00:07:33,495
he could read,
although clumsily.

157
00:07:34,746 --> 00:07:37,374
I'm attempting
to teach Chou-u as well,

158
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:40,168
but so far,
the brat's shown zero interest.

159
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:41,169
[grumbles]

160
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:52,138
Done.
I'll get to delivering it now.

161
00:07:52,222 --> 00:07:53,139
Right.

162
00:07:55,684 --> 00:07:57,560
I think this is going to work.

163
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:58,728
-[paws pattering]
-Mm?

164
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:00,689
[meowing]

165
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:02,482
[exclaiming]

166
00:08:03,108 --> 00:08:05,443
it's good to see you,
but why are you here?

167
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:07,404
[meows]

168
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:09,864
Come back, Maomao!

169
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,324
Why'd you run away?

170
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:13,535
[panting]

171
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:15,620
Oh, naughty kitty.
Running from Papa.

172
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,622
Oh. Little lady.

173
00:08:17,706 --> 00:08:19,833
Long time no see. [groans]

174
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:21,042
Uh.

175
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,170
[gulping]

176
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:26,131
Ah!

177
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:28,842
Oh, that mad dash
left me breathless.

178
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:31,052
Welcome. Now explain.

179
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:33,012
Shouldn't you be at work?

180
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:34,305
[gasps]

181
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:36,766
He must have
finally gotten fired.

182
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:38,017
The quack's a nice guy,

183
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:39,978
but totally worthless
as a doctor.

184
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:41,563
Forget I asked.

185
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:43,106
I'm confused.

186
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:45,525
Perhaps there's been
a slight misunderstanding.

187
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:47,527
I was allowed
to take a vacation,

188
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:50,488
and planned to visit my family
during my time away.

189
00:08:50,572 --> 00:08:52,073
I see.

190
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:53,616
They're sending you back home.

191
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:56,244
You're doing this on purpose,
aren't you?

192
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:58,538
I had to agree
to a curious stipulation

193
00:08:58,621 --> 00:08:59,998
if I wanted to take my trip.

194
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,292
I don't suppose they have talked
to you about it yet.

195
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:05,003
Mm. Nobody's told me.

196
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:06,463
Well, you see,

197
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:09,257
apparently another individual
wants to come along.

198
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,468
The head of the eunuchs
gave me the news.

199
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:13,595
It sounds like
someone important.

200
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:16,556
I was told to meet them here
before leaving for home.

201
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:17,891
That's interesting.

202
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:21,436
I was hoping
I'd be afforded more time.

203
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,858
[JINSHI] I'm going on a trip.
Come with me.

204
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:31,070
[MAOMAO] Master Jinshi's message
was pretty vague.

205
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:32,822
There was nothing
about the duration,

206
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:35,492
destination,
or even a departure date.

207
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:39,329
So, I taught Sazen medicine
as quickly as I could.

208
00:09:40,038 --> 00:09:41,039
Not to mention,

209
00:09:41,498 --> 00:09:43,291
prepped a stockpile
of ingredients in advance.

210
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:44,334
It's strange.

211
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:46,002
Of all people,

212
00:09:46,086 --> 00:09:47,837
why travel
with the quack doctor?

213
00:09:47,921 --> 00:09:48,797
And also...

214
00:09:49,798 --> 00:09:51,674
-A cat! How adorable.
-Oh!

215
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,301
-[women exclaiming]
-[hisses]

216
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:54,761
[both gasp]

217
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:57,138
Wait, come back here!

218
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:58,306
♪

219
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,516
[KYOU-U] That's what
I call a snack!

220
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:01,976
-[paws pattering]
-[BOTH] Huh?

221
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:03,853
-[screeches]
-[meows]

222
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:06,231
-[Zulin gasps]
-Wait, who invited you?

223
00:10:08,233 --> 00:10:09,150
[Kyou-u exclaims]

224
00:10:09,776 --> 00:10:10,693
Hey!

225
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:13,279
Whose cat even is this?!

226
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:14,656
The dining room.

227
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,283
[Kyou-u grumbles]

228
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,910
-[Guen panting]
-Huh?

229
00:10:20,787 --> 00:10:22,205
Who are you, old man?

230
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:25,208
I'm sorry
about the inconvenience.

231
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,544
Please, remember you're a guest,
Maomao.

232
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:28,962
[both laughing]

233
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,171
Wait, Maomao?

234
00:10:30,255 --> 00:10:31,589
What kind of name is that?

235
00:10:31,673 --> 00:10:32,632
[MAOMAO] A great one.

236
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,093
Now look after her.

237
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:39,472
-And keep her safe.
-Oh, you got it.

238
00:10:40,849 --> 00:10:44,185
I think it's best if I leave
sweet Maomao with my family.

239
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,564
Truth is, I'm the only one
in the rear palace

240
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:49,107
who can take care of her.

241
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:50,692
And besides,

242
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:53,319
Princess Lingli left
along with Empress Gyokuyou.

243
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:56,155
It seems they weren't allowed
to take the cat with them.

244
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,116
[MAOMAO] I guess
the idea got nixed

245
00:10:58,199 --> 00:10:59,659
by those around them.

246
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:02,036
There must be even more rules
outside the rear palace.

247
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,414
But my sister's glad.

248
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:06,416
She is eager
to put Maomao's skills

249
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,375
as a rat hunter to use.

250
00:11:09,127 --> 00:11:10,837
[MAOMAO] Is that the person
who sent you those letters

251
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,088
regarding paper-making?

252
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,174
That's correct.

253
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:17,677
But this time,
I found her correspondence

254
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,887
to be a bit concerning.

255
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:20,305
Why is that?

256
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,056
I shouldn't talk about it here.

257
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,601
I'll explain as soon as
we get to the village.

258
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:26,352
-[horse neighing]
-Oh.

259
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:31,774
[BASEN] Are you ready to leave?

260
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:36,613
[sighing uncomfortably]

261
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:39,490
Master Basen,
why are you dressed like--

262
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:40,700
[clears throat]

263
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:44,203
I just found out
I'm going today.

264
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,872
Why tell me at the last minute?

265
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:48,917
Trust us, we have our reasons.

266
00:11:48,999 --> 00:11:50,084
[MAOMAO] Reasons
important enough

267
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:51,586
to don disguises?

268
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,088
[sighs]

269
00:11:57,342 --> 00:11:58,885
Not a bad job.

270
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:01,429
He does look
like Master Basen's servant.

271
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:04,223
It's enough to fool the quack,
but that's not saying much.

272
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,601
Master Basen
doesn't seem comfortable

273
00:12:06,684 --> 00:12:07,644
in his role, though.

274
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:08,895
Now follow me.

275
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:11,648
You'll find your luggage
has been packed.

276
00:12:12,774 --> 00:12:13,900
Fine.

277
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,276
Something tells me

278
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,403
this is going to be
a long secret trip.

279
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:25,828
Given how busy he is,
this has to be inconvenient.

280
00:12:25,912 --> 00:12:29,082
The emperor sure likes putting
his little brother to work.

281
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,542
If I didn't know better,

282
00:12:31,626 --> 00:12:33,836
I'd say
he's training a successor--

283
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:36,839
Not gonna go there.

284
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,717
There's already a prince.

285
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:42,261
Lady Lihua gave birth
to a boy as well.

286
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:44,013
And the emperor's still young.

287
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:47,976
-[Guen humming]
-[horse neighing]

288
00:12:48,059 --> 00:12:49,269
Hmm.

289
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:53,439
[carriage rattling]

290
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,527
[MAOMAO] No sense thinking
disturbing thoughts.

291
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:05,201
After traveling two days
by horse carriage,

292
00:13:05,284 --> 00:13:07,120
we've reached
the quack's hometown,

293
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:09,205
southwest of the capital.

294
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:15,920
Those plants are barley.

295
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,674
[MAOMAO] The irrigation seems
very well developed here.

296
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:22,969
We use it
for rice farming in the summer.

297
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:24,137
Every year,

298
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,139
those are the two crops
that we grow,

299
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:28,933
and paddy rice can be grown
on the very same soil.

300
00:13:29,017 --> 00:13:30,643
It has nutrients to spare.

301
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:33,229
[MAOMAO] It's a fertile region,
no doubt.

302
00:13:33,313 --> 00:13:34,605
Plus, there's the river.

303
00:13:34,689 --> 00:13:36,315
Transportation must be good.

304
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:38,693
-[meowing]
-Uh.

305
00:13:39,277 --> 00:13:41,237
[MAOMAO] Doesn't look like
he's used to cats.

306
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:43,865
His list of weaknesses
grows ever longer.

307
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:46,034
Uh.

308
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,124
What was that look?

309
00:14:04,343 --> 00:14:06,345
-Oh.
-There's my dear brother.

310
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:08,222
Welcome back to your home.

311
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:09,557
[inhales deeply]

312
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,184
-Home. At long last.
-[meows]

313
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:13,269
The cat!

314
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:14,771
Let's see her.

315
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:16,898
[meows]

316
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,399
Aw, how cute.

317
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:19,734
She'll get along fine.

318
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:22,987
More importantly, I see
you brought guests with you.

319
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:25,239
Um, yes.

320
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,200
[GUEN'S SISTER]
So that explains it.

321
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:30,578
He's your superior,
and the girl's your assistant.

322
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:32,371
[MAOMAO] That kind of stings.

323
00:14:33,748 --> 00:14:35,792
Thank you for this.

324
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,335
Oh, it's nothing.

325
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:39,045
I just hope
you all enjoy your stay.

326
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:43,341
Wow.

327
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,592
Yes, please!

328
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:46,010
[GUEN'S SISTER]
Well, for a moment there,

329
00:14:46,094 --> 00:14:48,638
I thought my eunuch brother
settled down

330
00:14:48,721 --> 00:14:50,056
and had brought
his young wife back

331
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:52,141
to his village
to meet the rest of the family.

332
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:53,851
[laughs]

333
00:14:53,935 --> 00:14:55,311
I'm afraid that's impossible.

334
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:56,479
Got that right.

335
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:57,688
-[object clatters]
-[BOTH] Hmm?

336
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,819
[gasps]

337
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,322
[GUEN'S SISTER]
Are you all right?

338
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:07,657
I'll refill this.

339
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,624
[MAOMAO] If you wanted
to play a real servant,

340
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:17,917
you would have stayed
in the carriage

341
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,585
and eaten preserved foods.

342
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:22,046
Not like Master Basen
would allow that, though.

343
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:24,841
It'd be a shame
to ruin a decent disguise.

344
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:27,552
Hopefully, he doesn't do
anything to blow his cover.

345
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:28,678
-[door opens]
-[BASEN] Hmm?

346
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:29,887
I'm back, my dear.

347
00:15:29,971 --> 00:15:32,265
And we brought our appetites
with us!

348
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:35,101
Brother Guen!
It's been too long!

349
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:36,686
It's so good seeing you again.

350
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:38,855
The pleasure is all ours, Uncle.

351
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:42,066
My! Look how much
you've grown up.

352
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:44,068
[footsteps]

353
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:45,278
[man grunts angrily]

354
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:49,073
[grunts] Hmm.

355
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,368
[whimpers]

356
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:55,371
I swear! Have all your manners
gone right out the window?

357
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,290
What is with you?

358
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,293
[MAOMAO] So that's the quack's
other nephew.

359
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,254
The brothers don't seem
anything alike.

360
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,131
The man is a eunuch.

361
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:07,425
Well, if you can
even call him a man.

362
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:10,094
Why is he visiting
after all these years?

363
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,722
More than that,
are we going to ignore the fact

364
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:14,432
he brought some entourage
with him?

365
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:15,641
[GUEN'S SISTER]
Why would you say that?

366
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:17,518
[chuckles nervously]

367
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:19,645
[scoffs]

368
00:16:23,149 --> 00:16:24,025
Huh?

369
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:25,276
[Guen gasps nervously]

370
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:28,154
It's probably cold by now.
I'll take it.

371
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:30,031
[Guen's older nephew
gasps in disbelief]

372
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:31,949
Wha...

373
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:36,329
Where is my soup?

374
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,289
Don't you have
something to say first?

375
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:40,291
[grumbles]

376
00:16:43,044 --> 00:16:44,337
To hell with this.

377
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,755
I apologize.

378
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,256
The boy doesn't seem
to understand

379
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,966
how hard you've worked
and what you sacrificed

380
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:50,384
for this village.

381
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:52,386
You really shouldn't worry.

382
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:55,056
Seriously,
I'm used to this sort of thing.

383
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:56,933
[Guen's sister sighs]

384
00:16:57,642 --> 00:16:58,935
[MAOMAO] If I remember right,

385
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:01,270
the quack doctor went to work
at the rear palace

386
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:02,647
in his sister's stead.

387
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,398
It clearly still affects her.

388
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:06,984
So?

389
00:17:07,068 --> 00:17:08,736
[MAOMAO] Hmm? Mm.

390
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:10,571
-[gasps]
-[sighs]

391
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:13,991
M-Madam, I apologize
for showing up without warning.

392
00:17:15,243 --> 00:17:16,577
Good. Then all's well.

393
00:17:16,911 --> 00:17:19,455
Now then, you reached out to me
because you needed something?

394
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:22,291
I take it we have
important matters to discuss.

395
00:17:22,959 --> 00:17:25,419
[sighs] The truth is,

396
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:27,797
we have a request that we wish
to beg of the emperor!

397
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,423
What?

398
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,968
You could ask. After all,
you're the great doctor

399
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,469
who helped birth
his children, right?

400
00:17:33,553 --> 00:17:34,971
-[exclaims]
-[chokes]

401
00:17:37,807 --> 00:17:39,725
[Guen whimpering]

402
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,730
[MAOMAO] My dad deserves
the credit for that.

403
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:47,316
I guess
he's been exaggerating his part.

404
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,069
Naturally,
I would never out him, but...

405
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,114
these two are doing
a pretty good job.

406
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:56,534
Me? I'm in no place to ask
for an audience with him.

407
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:58,160
That's far beyond my station.

408
00:17:58,828 --> 00:17:59,996
Is there truly no way?

409
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:04,792
Look, I... I'd never be able
to see the emperor,

410
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:07,420
but there are others
I may be able to talk to.

411
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:09,213
W-What does this concern?

412
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:10,423
[BOTH] Hmm.

413
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:12,842
[Basen groans]

414
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,760
-[MAOMAO] Mm.
-[gasps]

415
00:18:14,844 --> 00:18:15,803
[clears throat]

416
00:18:16,971 --> 00:18:18,639
Please speak freely around us.

417
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,100
I don't know
how much help we can be, but...

418
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:22,685
Go on ahead.

419
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:25,563
These are proper officials
who might be able to assist you.

420
00:18:27,148 --> 00:18:28,399
If you say so.

421
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:33,988
[GUEN'S BROTHER-IN-LAW] The
matter pertains to the village,

422
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:36,407
specifically the rights
to the land it was built on.

423
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,994
As it turns out, originally,
the plot was borrowed.

424
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:42,246
[MAOMAO]
According to the husband,

425
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:44,790
the previous landlord
was a very generous man

426
00:18:44,874 --> 00:18:47,084
and let the villagers
rent the land at a bargain

427
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:48,252
since he wasn't using it.

428
00:18:48,878 --> 00:18:50,004
Time passed,

429
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:52,298
and eventually, the conversation
turned from leasing

430
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:54,759
to the villagers
actually purchasing the land.

431
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:59,055
They signed a contract making
the land and forest theirs

432
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:00,848
over the next 20 years.

433
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:03,392
Payment proceeded
without any issue.

434
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:09,523
But a few years ago,
the landlord passed away.

435
00:19:09,607 --> 00:19:13,027
When his son took over,
things quickly went downhill.

436
00:19:14,195 --> 00:19:17,073
It turned out the new landlord
despised outsiders

437
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:20,034
and had a general disrespect
for all craftsmen.

438
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,161
Furthermore, he was vexed

439
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:24,580
that their paper made them
purveyors to the emperor.

440
00:19:25,206 --> 00:19:27,583
And after the one time
paper quality went down,

441
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:28,918
he used that as an excuse

442
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:30,795
to keep demanding payment
on the loan.

443
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,673
For a long while, he's claimed
we dirtied the water

444
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:36,133
and ruined the yields.

445
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:37,927
Or that we use too much water,

446
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:40,137
and now they can't even grow
their own rice.

447
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:43,349
We've always been able to
tolerate his harassment.

448
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:45,601
But this is different.

449
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,645
Things have gotten
way more serious.

450
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:49,063
We have to pay now,

451
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:51,399
or he is going to force us
to leave immediately.

452
00:19:52,525 --> 00:19:54,485
How many years of payment
do you have left?

453
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,487
Only five.

454
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:59,240
But there's no way we can pay it
in one lump sum.

455
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,658
And our new landlord,

456
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,785
he wants to take over
all the paper-making.

457
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,662
I don't understand.

458
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:06,372
Why won't he
let us do our trade?

459
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,332
Because of the new tax.

460
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:11,710
Just recently, the taxes
increased on all grains.

461
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:14,004
[GUEN'S BROTHER-IN-LAW]
Meanwhile, the tax

462
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:16,298
on paper-making went down
a few years ago.

463
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:18,551
I'm sure that
only aggravates him further.

464
00:20:20,136 --> 00:20:21,637
[MAOMAO] The tax cut
must have been in order

465
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,013
to increase literacy.

466
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:25,975
Meanwhile, the hike on grains

467
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:28,269
must be due to
the looming locust plague.

468
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:31,522
Given the double crop yield
from this region,

469
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:34,775
the tax hike shouldn't be enough
to cause any real problems.

470
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:39,905
Regardless, it can't be easy
being on the receiving end.

471
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,324
And on top of that,

472
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:44,243
there's a problem
closer to home.

473
00:20:44,994 --> 00:20:48,080
My older son sided with
the farmers for a few reasons.

474
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:51,250
He believes bureaucrats are all
the same and won't help us.

475
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:54,545
That's why we wanted to see
if it was at all possible

476
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:56,755
for you to ask
about a tax cut on grains.

477
00:20:58,966 --> 00:21:02,136
I would, but who'd even listen
to a eunuch like me?

478
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:04,638
We understand.

479
00:21:06,891 --> 00:21:10,144
In that case, tomorrow,
we're all having a discussion.

480
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:11,228
You can come as well.

481
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:13,272
I would like that.

482
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:15,232
-[BASEN] May I join as well?
-Hmm?

483
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:20,946
It's just, the other party
might not approve.

484
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:22,990
I would have
an outside perspective.

485
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,492
That could be quite valuable.

486
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:26,702
I won't interject.

487
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:29,622
If they do end up refusing me,
I'll speak to them.

488
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:32,374
[MAOMAO] I guess he's concerned,
since he's involved.

489
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,960
If you'd like. All right.

490
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:36,754
You had better believe

491
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:38,589
I'm gonna be
in attendance as well!

492
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:41,383
[MAOMAO] You won't be
of much use, but good for you.

493
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,302
[crickets chirping]

494
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,805
♪

495
00:21:48,474 --> 00:21:50,309
[woman crying]

496
00:21:52,353 --> 00:21:53,938
[GUEN'S OLDER NEPHEW]
Please stop crying.

497
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,397
Dry those eyes.

498
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:58,692
[WOMAN] It's just,
at this rate...

499
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:02,947
Don't you worry.

500
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:05,658
I'll take care of everything.

501
00:22:06,242 --> 00:22:08,285
[crying]

502
00:22:12,373 --> 00:22:13,832
[sighs]

503
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,961
[♪ closing theme song playing]

504
00:23:45,633 --> 00:23:47,259
♪

505
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,519
[NARRATOR] Next time, "The Bet."

